-- title:
--   A scalar-normalized translation has the exact character covariance
-- statement:
--   Let $h$ be an absolutely summable real sequence, and let $V$ be an actual unitary from the distinguished induced corner to the translated-corner Hilbert space. Suppose its representative formula is
--   $$(Vu)(p)=a\,u(F_h(p))\quad\text{almost everywhere},$$
--   with $a\in\mathbb R$ and the explicit corner translation $F_h$. Then for every compact parameter $k$, character $i$ and source vector $u$,
--   $$V M_{k,i}u=M^{\mathrm{translated}}_{k+\iota(h),i}Vu.$$
--   The statement verifies the needed covariance from the actual pullback formula.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Comparisons of benchmark equivalence relations, Theorem 1.5 (formerly MeasureEquivalence.tex, Theorem 1.3); supporting declaration MeasureEquivalenceRestrictedPhase.normalizedTranslation_phase_intertwines in RestrictedTranslationIntertwining.lean, lines 33–59; local source SHA-256 52bc52d018ad2f00daa7187067e2d53ba7efb13db3a58cc89a60bdb0826d5c87. Designated upload repository: https://github.com/RayjunWang/Benchmark (no source commit published yet).

